  "code": "BKQP",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Clinical Significance</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Not Detected</strong></td>\n<td>No BK virus DNA detected in the sample</td>\n<td>No evidence of active BK virus infection at the time of testing</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Detected (Positive)</strong></td>\n<td>BK virus DNA detected</td>\n<td>Indicates <strong>active infection</strong> or <strong>reactivation</strong> of BK virus. Requires correlation with clinical status and, if relevant, <strong>quantitative PCR</strong> to assess viral load.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"608\" data-end=\"686\">\n<p data-start=\"610\" data-end=\"686\"><strong data-start=\"610\" data-end=\"622\">BK virus</strong> is a polyomavirus that usually remains latent in the kidneys.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"687\" data-end=\"842\">\n<p data-start=\"689\" data-end=\"842\">Reactivation typically occurs in <strong data-start=\"722\" data-end=\"752\">immunocompromised patients</strong> (especially kidney transplant recipients, hematopoietic stem cell transplant patients).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"843\" data-end=\"1030\">\n<p data-start=\"845\" data-end=\"878\">Clinical conditions associated:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"881\" data-end=\"1030\">\n<li data-start=\"881\" data-end=\"952\">\n<p data-start=\"883\" data-end=\"952\"><strong data-start=\"883\" data-end=\"907\">BK virus nephropathy</strong> (renal dysfunction in transplant patients)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"955\" data-end=\"1030\">\n<p data-start=\"957\" data-end=\"1030\"><strong data-start=\"957\" data-end=\"981\">Hemorrhagic cystitis</strong> (in bone marrow/stem cell transplant patients)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1031\" data-end=\"1090\">\n<p data-start=\"1033\" data-end=\"1090\"><strong data-start=\"1033\" data-end=\"1052\">Qualitative PCR</strong> only tells <strong data-start=\"1064\" data-end=\"1087\">presence or absence</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1091\" data-end=\"1234\">\n<p data-start=\"1093\" data-end=\"1234\">If <strong data-start=\"1096\" data-end=\"1108\">positive</strong>, a <strong data-start=\"1112\" data-end=\"1157\">Quantitative PCR (viral load measurement)</strong> is usually done to monitor disease activity and guide treatment decisions.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
